ess notifications are shown inside the mutation hook in the feature's api/ folder (in onSuccess)\"\n\nIs this a rule OR an observation of what's wrong? The feedback says \"it breaks two project rules\". The sentences after the colon describe what the code review found and what the rules say.\n\nI think the rules are:\nRule 1: Success notifications ARE to be shown inside the mutation hook (api/ folder, in onSuccess). Feature components MUST NOT call useNotifications.\nRule 2: Query keys come from the query options. Literal arrays only inside queryOptions.\n\nThe violations would be:\nViolation 1: Feature components call useNotifications (when they shouldn't). The fix is to move the notification logic into the mutation hook's onSuccess.\nViolation 2: Using literal query arrays in `invalidateQueries` (when they should use `getQueryOptions().queryKey`).\n\nBut I haven't found literal query arrays outside of queryOptions in the api/ files. All of them use `getQueryOptions().queryKey`.\n\nLet me look at the feature components more carefully, specifically the create-comment and create-discussion files:","thinkingSignature":"reasoning"},{"type":"text","text":"Let me read the feature component files that use `useNotifications`:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_ags0i4km","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"apps/react-vite/src/features/comments/components/create-comment.tsx"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_hk4ofs95","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"apps/react-vite/src/features/discussions/components/create-discussion.tsx"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_85exksr1","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"apps/react-vite/src/features/discussions/components/delete-discussion.tsx"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"ollama","model":"qwen3.6:35b-a3b-coding","usage":{"input":27,"output":2493,"cacheRead":40063,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":42583,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":false}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timesta