g?: MutationConfig\\u003ctypeof deleteUser\\u003e;\\n};\\n\\nexport const useDeleteUser = ({\\n  mutationConfig,\\n}: UseDeleteUserOptions = {}) =\\u003e {\\n  const queryClient = useQueryClient();\\n\\n  const { onSuccess, ...restConfig } = mutationConfig || {};\\n\\n  return useMutation({\\n    onSuccess: (...args) =\\u003e {\\n      queryClient.invalidateQueries({\\n        queryKey: getUsersQueryOptions().queryKey,\\n      });\\n      onSuccess?.(...args);\\n    },\\n    ...restConfig,\\n    mutationFn: deleteUser,\\n  });\\n};\"}]}"}}
{"type":"message_update","usage":{"input":554,"output":1527,"cacheRead":50193,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":52274,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0,"totalFromProvider":false}},"assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"The notification store only exports `useNotifications` which is a Zustand store. To add a notification from a non-React context (like a mutation hook), you'd typically use the store's `addNotification` function directly.\n\nLet me check if there's a way to call the store outside of a component. In Zustand, you can call `getState()` or access the store's methods by importing the store class.\n\nActually, looking at the store definition:\n```typescript\nexport const useNotifications = create<NotificationsStore>((set) => ({\n  notifications: [],\n  addNotification: (notification) => ...\n  dismissNotification: (id) => ...\n}));\n```\n\nThe store is exported as a React hook (due to `create`), but you can also access the `addNotification` method directly by calling `useNotifications.setState(...)`. But that requires using the setState method which is provided by Zustand.\n\nWait, in Zustand you can:\n1. Import the store and call `store.setState(...)`\n2. Or access the `addNotification` function by extracting it.\n\nActually, with `create`, the returned object has a `setState` method. But we need `addNotification` directly. Let me check if there's another way.\n\nIn Zustand, you can do:\n```javascript\nimport { useNotifications } from './notifications-store';\n\nuseNotifications.getState().addNotification({...});\n```\n\nOr you can export a function. Let me check if there's a pattern in the codebase for this.\n\nActually, looking at the mutation hooks, they already use `onSuccess: (...args) => { ... }`. So they can call `useNotifications.getState().addNotification({...})` inside the `onSuccess` handler.\n\nBut wait, calling `useNotifications.getState()` from inside a non-React function (like the `onSuccess` callback in `useMutation`) might be problematic if the hook hasn't been initialized.\n\nLet me check if there's a better pattern. Actually, in the Zustand library, you can access the state without being inside a React component by using `getState()`:\n```javascript\nimport { useNotifications } from './notifications-store';\n\nuseNotifications.getState().addNotification({ type: 'success', title: '...' });\n```\n\nHowever, this might fail if the store hasn't been initialized yet. Let me check if there's a way to make it work.\n\nActually, since the store is created with `create`, the `addNotification` method is part of the store's initial state. So `useNotifications.getState().addNotification` would work even outside of React.\n\nLet me now make the changes.\n\nFirst, let me identify all the api/ files that need to be updated:\n\n1. **`apps/react-vite/src/features/users/api/delete-user.ts`** - Add notification for \"User Deleted\"\n2. **`apps/react-vite/src/features/users/api/update-user-role.ts`** - Add notification for \"User Role Updated\"\n3. **`apps/react-vite/src/features/users/api/update-profile.ts`** - Add notification for \"Profile Updated\"\n4. **`apps/react-vite/src/features/discussions/api/create-discussion.ts`** - Add notification for \"Discussion Created\"\n5. **`apps/react-vite/src/features/discussions/api/delete-discussion.ts`** - Add notification for \"Discussion Deleted\"\n6. **`apps/react-vite/src/features/discussions/api/update-discussion.ts`** - Add notification for \"Discussion Updated\"\n7. **`apps/react-vite/src/features/comments/api/create-comment.ts`** - Add notification for \"Comment Created\"\n8. **`apps/react-vite/src/features/comments/api/delete-comment.ts`** - Add notification for \"Comment Deleted\"\n\nNow let me read each file and update them:"}}
